# Component folders

Every component is a kebab-case folder. The same shape applies at every nesting level.

```
{name}/
  {name}.tsx       — one component; props interface in this file
  styles.ts
  index.ts
  types.ts         — non-prop types only, and only when they exist
  constants.ts     — closed-set values only, and only when they exist
  {name}.stories.tsx
  ui/{child}/      — every nested component, same shape
  lib/             — pure helpers used only by this component
  tests/           — every test for this folder: the component and each lib/ helper
```

- Folder and implementation file are kebab-case of the export: `Button` → `button/button.tsx`, `CustomButton` → `custom-button/custom-button.tsx`. Never `Button.tsx` or `itemCard.tsx`.
- One component per file. A second component is `{name}/ui/{child}/`, not a sibling file and not a second component in the parent file. The only exception is a file that configures an external library's compound parts: a re-homed shadcn/Radix primitive keeps `Dialog`, `DialogTrigger`, `DialogContent`, and the rest in one file.
- The props `interface` is declared in the component file, above the component. It does not go in `types.ts`. Other types do: component-local non-prop types (a view union, a row model) live in that folder's `types.ts`; domain types live in the slice model folder (`features/*/models/types.ts`, `entities/*/model/types.ts`). Do not add `types.ts` when the props interface was the only type. A `VariantProps` type derived from `cva` stays in `styles.ts`.
- Helpers and view mappers used only by this component live in `{name}/lib/`. No `let` and no IIFE in the component file. DTO mappers stay in the slice `api/`. Slice-wide helpers stay in the slice `lib/`. Do not drop `mapX.ts` or `formatX.ts` next to `{name}.tsx`.
- `{name}.stories.tsx` sits beside `{name}.tsx`. Every test for the folder lives in `{name}/tests/`: `{name}.test.tsx` and a test for each `lib/` helper. Not beside the source file.
- `styles.ts`, `index.ts`, `types.ts`, and `constants.ts` keep those exact names. `constants.ts` holds the closed-set values a caller passes as props (`ButtonVariant`, `ButtonType`).
- The named export is PascalCase (`export const CustomButton`). Import the folder through `index.ts`, never the `.tsx` file.
- A component folder's `index.ts` exports the component. It exports the props type or a constant only when a file outside the folder imports it. Nothing else is exported "for later".

For scaffolding the folder, load the `react-component` skill.
